From: Your Name <your.email@example.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: Add NPU power domain regulator for RK3568

The RK3568 NPU power domain requires VDD_NPU regulator to be enabled
before power domain operations. Add the domain-supply property to the
NPU power domain node so the pm-domains driver can manage the regulator.

This is required for proper NPU power domain management on boards like
the Radxa ROCK 3B that have a dedicated VDD_NPU regulator.

Signed-off-by: Your Name <your.email@example.com>
---
Note: This patch shows the concept. The actual implementation depends on
how the board DTS defines the vdd_npu regulator. Each board may need a
specific patch to add the domain-supply binding.

For rk3568-rock-3b.dts, the vdd_npu regulator is DCDC_REG4 from the RK809
PMIC. The binding would be added to the power-controller node.

Example for ROCK 3B:

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-rock-3b.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-rock-3b.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-rock-3b.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-rock-3b.dts
@@ -xxx,6 +xxx,14 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };

+/* Add regulator supply for NPU power domain */
+&power {
+	pd_npu: power-domain@1 {
+		reg = <RK3568_PD_NPU>;
+		domain-supply = <&vdd_npu>;
+	};
+};
+
 &pmu_io_domains {
 	pmuio1-supply = <&vcc3v3_pmu>;
 	pmuio2-supply = <&vcc3v3_pmu>;

---
Alternative approach - add to power-controller directly:

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x.dtsi
@@ -xxx,6 +xxx,12 @@
 		power: power-controller {
 			compatible = "rockchip,rk3568-power-controller";
 			#power-domain-cells = <1>;
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <0>;
+
+			power-domain@1 {
+				reg = <RK3568_PD_NPU>;
+				/* domain-supply set by board DTS */
+			};
 		};
 	};

Then in board DTS (rk3568-rock-3b.dts):

+&power {
+	/delete-node/ power-domain@1;
+
+	power-domain@1 {
+		reg = <RK3568_PD_NPU>;
+		domain-supply = <&vdd_npu>;
+	};
+};

